hello and welcome to the very first  episode of deep dive the brand new  podcast that delves into the minds of  entrepreneurs creators and other  inspiring people to uncover their  journeys towards finding joy and  fulfillment at work and in life my name  is ali and in each episode i chat to my  guests about the philosophy strategies  and tools that have helped them along  the path to living a life of happiness  and meaning so that was the intro for  the new podcast that we're launching  welcome to deep dive whether you are  watching this on the youtube channel or  listening to this on a podcast app it is  lovely to see you if you don't know me  then hi my name is ali i'm a doctor  youtuber and podcaster currently living  in london and this podcast has been a  long-term ambition dream of mine to have  a sort of podcast where i've basically  got an excuse to have a long form  conversation with people who i admire  and the cool thing about a podcast like  this is that we can really showcase  other people's expertise and other  people's journeys for the last four  years since 2017 i've been making videos  on youtube about how to live a healthier  happier more productive life and it's  been mostly sharing my own personal  experience but also the experience of  authors through books and book summaries  and all that kind of stuff if you're not  familiar with my main channel there will  be a link in the video description and  then the show notes all that fun stuff  but the really cool thing about a  podcast is that i can now have these  conversations with people from all  around the world who are thriving in  their fields whether it be  entrepreneurialism or creatorism or i  don't know just other cool cool kind of  stuff and in particular i'm very  interested in how these cool people find  fulfillment in work and in life and so  we've got a lot of interviews with  entrepreneurs who made it like really  successful by society's traditional  definitions of success and we kind of  dive into what their early days were  like how they set up a company like  gymshark or my protein how they how they  got it off the ground how they kept  themselves motivated in the early days  when nothing seemed to be working how  they made it fun for themselves along  the way the successes along the way the  failures along the way what they learned  from that journey and how they're  thinking about what they're doing with  their lives moving forward often the  people that we've interviewed have had  traditional success and in a way like  figuring out what to do with your life  once you've ticked the boxes of societal  success is  an interesting problem as well in  addition to the the thing of getting  something started from the ground up  hopefully the interviews and  conversations will be interesting to  listen to uh and will be inspiring uh at  whatever stage you are of your journey  and certainly they've been inspiring for  me so far the ones that we've done for  season one and hopefully they'll also  have some practical and actionable  advice that you can apply to your own  life as well um one thing i say in the  intro is that we do want to be taking  everything that people say with a little  sprinkle of salt i think it's important  to keep in mind when you listen to a  podcast like this one which is often  based around self-help or advice giving  that you know people like me people like  our guests as successful as the guests  are by societies whatever metrics  society wants to use as successful as  they are they can only really speak to  their own personal experience and  certainly when i speak for my youtube  videos or in this podcast i'm just  sharing my own personal experience and  so it's easy to get into that mindset of  like oh this is this is like solid  advice and this person knows what  they're talking about therefore i should  listen to their advice i think that's  fine but i think when it comes to life  advice it's it's more a case of see what  works for different people and then take  the bits that resonate with you and  apply those to your own life because as  much as we'd like it like there really  is no manual for living a happy and  meaningful life there are certainly you  know evidence-based things that we can  do to help along the way and that's a  lot of the stuff that we're going to be  sharing on the podcast but there's no  clear manual and i think if there was  then life would just be a little bit  boring so that's why i say take  everything that you hear on this podcast  with a little sprinkle of salt to be on  that i hope you find the interviews the  conversations insightful and  entertaining and informative and all  those other adjectives if this sounds  good if you'd like to support the  podcast then really everything is free  um we might have sponsors further down  the line if sponsors want to reach out  to us but basically if you can just like  subscribe to the podcast feed on your  podcast app of choice whether that's  itunes or apple podcast or google  podcast or spotify or wherever you're  listening to this hit the subscribe  button or if you're watching this on our  youtube channel do hit the subscribe  button as well we also have a deep dive  clips youtube channel where we take like  sound bites and snippets from the  conversation and hopefully give them a  good title and thumbnail and put that on  the clips channel because i know  sometimes you know an hour to three hour  long conversation it's hard to make the  time to listen to those sorts of things  even if you do listen to this stuff at  2x speed uh like i sometimes like to do  and so you might like to check out the  deep dive clips channel as well but yeah  thank you so much for watching uh this  or listening to this intro uh hopefully  you'll find the interviews  good and i guess we'll  see you sometime in the podcast feed i  don't really know how to do a podcast  it's all it's all a bit new but it's all  pretty exciting so yeah thanks for  watching slash listening and and see you  later bye

